<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro lands in Miami after fleeing Brazil for US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bd1348dee84865d5a80693b41a7539dec3048039106a9d3a5035a04469c4491</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil-for-us/a-79788659--9753c6724576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil-for-us/a-79788659?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family landed in Florida early on Wednesday. Facing money laundering allegations, he fled just days after refusing to concede defeat to incumbent Lula.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain train crash caused by operator 'inexplicably' telling driver to resume journey despite red signal, transport minister says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fec49b87a51854623e9b46316a41c5b165624ad95c1a4cec64641c211a40ad93</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-train-crash-caused-by-operator-inexplicably-telling-driver-to-resume-journey-despite-red-signa/live-79785087--e3139585dc3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-train-crash-caused-by-operator-inexplicably-telling-driver-to-resume-journey-despite-red-signal-transport-minister-says/live-79785087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two high-speed trains carrying hundreds of passengers collided south of Madrid. Spain's transport minister said one of the trains was told to continue its journey despite a "red signal" being in effect. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5ed55643657f7a62530839ab7bca82dbf29ca635b456b4387ac653388ed2f6c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests in Germany: Is France-style violence looming?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e255b48bdebdbfbe4c12041de106c69670b7c865af399b1c98efd1a493a4946c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050--fb575275c7ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Young people in Germany will take to the streets this weekend to demand education and action on climate change. Politicians warn that the protests could become violent, as in France, but the situations are different.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Israel election: Netanyahu-led bloc in slight lead with more than 80% of votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0e8ce2321cbbe273b88f281b9a797d436a8c110b86ec92f171d4e9552556d6d</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-election-netanyahu-led-bloc-in-slight-lead-with-more-than-80-of-votes-counted/live-79713839--ce4e0610679a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-election-netanyahu-led-bloc-in-slight-lead-with-more-than-80-of-votes-counted/live-79713839?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While partial results show the pro-Netanyahu bloc ahead of the anti-Netanyahu bloc, the final tally could take days. Neither grouping is expected to win a majority, with tough coalition talks ahead. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17104b5db60cd74f0ca5c2ae5d662194806b61a97fc03da23e42158928d66903</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62d1717c1d1b335610ae582be343625451931a678505369639966a28ddcb0dec</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parties debate who should succeed President Steinmeier, with several women under discussion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57def128fa39cdb362bf957ad01f086030837101d589e295c54dc91f8706f8f8</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discuss/live-79783779--1c6d43c0de10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parties-debate-who-should-succeed-president-steinmeier-with-several-women-under-discussion/live-79783779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's political parties are weighing possible successors to President Frank-Walter Steinmeier, with no candidate agreed yet. Meanwhile, a poll suggests most Germans are giving Halloween a miss this year. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2665e7cc52fe84e49bfdf51994cb6cff959018671c14465699b0d3d90389ddb9</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens of people killed after high-speed trains collide in central Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f9ed0de36448011a5bddabe24b9c79572cd904b53f15b95358c411143804827</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-of-people-killed-after-high-speed-trains-collide-in-central-spain/a-79784119--b7f767ed615f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-of-people-killed-after-high-speed-trains-collide-in-central-spain/a-79784119?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 68 people have been killed in a train crash in central Spain, local authorities have confirmed. Rail services between Madrid and Seville have been suspended.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:114e420152a4db880f959ff8c5437a5162935a307739406e027beb1ccc0e305b</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian police shoot dead assailant at Israeli Embassy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c835d9ae1d507688deddc63bd53aaf0c3d59f77879ca4d938b2bc1f80881a5c4</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905--d152a4aa69fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A "minor" has been killed by police after attacking a guard at Israel's embassy in Belgrade with knives, the interior minister says. Ivica Dacic said police had declared the highest terror alert after the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cyclone Arnab turns deadly after landfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8fceb225deb4e2691b33d709800f0716f16f5c3183dbc4dd37aa8ea5f2243af</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T04:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323--51b97fb16b83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Arnab killed at least three people in Andhra Pradesh after making landfall earlier today. Also, a new report says India is paying a steep economic cost over heat. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Experts urge 'global health emergency' as climate harms accelerate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8442add2fbe2cbe0e1ddd2cee6d92083ef777cb6bd2892104a609145be59f4e0</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T00:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/experts-urge-global-health-emergency-as-climate-harms-accelerate/a-79773232--6973c15b8839.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/experts-urge-global-health-emergency-as-climate-harms-accelerate/a-79773232?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Lancet report reveals the growing toll of climate change on human health, from rising heat deaths and drought to food insecurity and lost livelihoods.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt orders closure of independent news site Mada Masr</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fb30d326ff27fb03383b41a628d75e4f3bdedf17026557843bd50b90983a95e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842--499fd97538eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Editor-in-chief Lina Attalah was briefly detained and fined over licensing violations. Rights groups condemned the ruling as a major blow to press freedom in Egypt, where independent media face growing pressure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US amid investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f842eb3fe9c8b95fa37dccdb1ede21491984619ec285cb37e96ac495083346f5</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T22:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-amid-investigation/a-79781094--17bcb76430fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-amid-investigation/a-79781094?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro, who lost to incumbent Lula in Sunday's presidential election, has reportedly fled the country. Bolsonaro, who is facing multiple corruption probes, has refused to concede.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes giving Frontex border agency new major powers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d07f634d0ac53411bf2ff75e1e4c250f0a54adca95a8186d5f83327979871524</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-giving-frontex-border-agency-new-major-powers/a-79779690--2177a1c8ad5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-giving-frontex-border-agency-new-major-powers/a-79779690?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has unveiled a new plan to give Frontex more resources to ensure the return of irregular migrants, including by supporting non-EU countries. The move comes after the tragedy in Ceuta.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mbappe apologizes as Chinese sponsors drop him and TV broadcasts are halted over Mao dictator remark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:083b4097fbc485a5d3e300e74802820ffff2bdba10b41d8dae0f1f8c8e0ec306</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831--140a68dc18a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French soccer star Kylian Mbappe has apologized after apparently referring to Mao Zedong as a dictator. Chinese sponsors have dropped him, while state television has suspended Spanish league broadcasts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e10d8aed82ff1e8466763c917de11a7108685303f746befac393b15715c03742</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd88968447adafde6b8e27a7b44ccae39a59d5d5bdd29a901d782116fc102cba</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
